# Ente Doctor Backend — Core Stack & Tooling

## Repository Identity

- This is `ente-doctor-backend`, a **pnpm 10 workspaces** monorepo. No Nx, Turborepo, or Lerna exist or are permitted.
- Workspace globs are defined in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`: `apps/*` and `packages/*`.
- The authoritative human-readable guide is [DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md](../../DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md). When intent is unclear, defer to it.

## Stack

- **Runtime:** Node.js 22 (Alpine in Docker). Target ES2023.
- **Language:** TypeScript 5.7+ with `module`/`moduleResolution: NodeNext`.
- **Framework:** NestJS 11 (`@nestjs/common`, `@nestjs/core`, `@nestjs/config`, `@nestjs/microservices`, `@nestjs/platform-express`).
- **Messaging:** Apache Kafka via `kafkajs` only. Never introduce gRPC or `*.proto` files.
- **Persistence:** PostgreSQL 16 — one isolated database per domain service. Redis 7 for caching.

## Shell Command Invocation

> **Critical for AI agents running shell commands.**

`pnpm` is managed by **Corepack** on this machine and is not on the system `PATH` as a standalone binary. Every shell command that calls `pnpm` **must** be prefixed with `corepack`:

```powershell
# ✅ Correct — always use this form
corepack pnpm install
corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/auth-service add bcryptjs
corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/notification-service add -D nodemon

# ❌ Wrong — pnpm is not on PATH
pnpm install
```

This applies to **every** pnpm invocation in a terminal/shell tool call: `install`, `add`, `remove`, `run`, `exec`, `dlx`, and filter commands.

## Tooling Bans

- **Never** invoke `npm`, `yarn`, or `npx`. Always use `corepack pnpm`, `corepack pnpm dlx`, or `corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<name>`.
- **Never** add Nx, Turborepo, or Lerna files/configs.
- **Never** create a `.nvmrc` or `.node-version` that disagrees with Node 22.

## Canonical Scripts

Only invoke these root scripts; never invent new top-level names (all prefixed with `corepack`):

- `corepack pnpm install` — install workspace dependencies.
- `corepack pnpm docker:up` / `corepack pnpm docker:down` / `corepack pnpm docker:logs` — control the local infra (`docker-compose.yml`).
- `corepack pnpm dev` — run all services in `tsx watch` mode in parallel.
- `corepack pnpm build` / `corepack pnpm lint` / `corepack pnpm test` / `corepack pnpm clean` — recursive operations via `corepack pnpm -r --filter @ente-doctor/*`.
- For single-app work, scope explicitly: `corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<app> <script>`.

## Dependency Hygiene

- **Never** install third-party dependencies at the workspace root. Always scope: `corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<app> add <pkg>`.
- Root `devDependencies` are a strict allowlist: `typescript`, `prettier`, `@types/node`, `tsx`. Never expand it.
- Per-service `devDependencies` may include `@swc/core`, `@swc-node/register`, and `nodemon` when the service uses SWC as its dev compiler (see rule `05-swc-compiler`).
- **Always** reference internal packages via `workspace:*`.
- **Never** pin patch versions manually. Let pnpm resolve.
- **Never** add a third-party package when an internal `@ente-doctor/*` package already covers the need.

## App Surface

The six deployable services in `apps/` are: `api-gateway` (3000), `auth-service` (3001), `provider-service` (3002), `booking-service` (3003), `search-service` (3004), `notification-service` (3005). The three shared packages are `@ente-doctor/common`, `@ente-doctor/contracts`, `@ente-doctor/event-bus`.
